Grammar

Rule 0     S' -> Prog
Rule 1     Prog -> BEGIN ListaSent END
Rule 2     ListaSent -> Sent ListaSent
Rule 3     ListaSent -> Sent
Rule 4     Sent -> Asig
Rule 5     Sent -> Impr
Rule 6     Sent -> Func
Rule 7     Asig -> ID ASIGNAR Expr
Rule 8     Impr -> PRINT ID
Rule 9     Func -> DEF ID SIMBOLO Exprt
Rule 10    Expr -> Exprt
Rule 11    Expr -> IF ID IN ID SIMBOLO Exprt ELSE SIMBOLO Exprt
Rule 12    Expr -> PARENT_ABRE PARENT_CIERRA
Rule 13    Exprt -> ID Oper ID
Rule 14    Oper -> CONCATENAR
Rule 15    Oper -> IN PARENT_ABRE CONSTANTE PARENT_CIERRA

Terminals, with rules where they appear

ASIGNAR              : 7
BEGIN                : 1
CONCATENAR           : 14
CONSTANTE            : 15
DEF                  : 9
ELSE                 : 11
END                  : 1
ID                   : 7 8 9 11 11 13 13
IF                   : 11
IN                   : 11 15
PARENT_ABRE          : 12 15
PARENT_CIERRA        : 12 15
PRINT                : 8
SIMBOLO              : 9 11 11
error                : 

Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

Asig                 : 4
Expr                 : 7
Exprt                : 9 10 11 11
Func                 : 6
Impr                 : 5
ListaSent            : 1 2
Oper                 : 13
Prog                 : 0
Sent                 : 2 3

Parsing method: LALR

